Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Iterated Finite Automata", "GuideTitle",
 CellID->626661274,ExpressionUUID->"b32903a4-6bf3-4f27-9451-c1155948304f"],

Cell["\<\
An iterated finite automaton applies a finite-state transducer (Mealy \
machine) repeatedly to a row of symbols: each pass reads the row from the \
left, rewriting it while updating the internal state, and iteration produces \
a spacetime evolution analogous to a cellular automaton. An invertible \
transducer instead acts on the rooted tree of words by automorphisms, and the \
states generate an automata group \[LongDash] the odometer, the lamplighter \
group and the Grigorchuk group among them. This paclet follows Andrzej Zuk's \
WSRI26 essay \"Iterated Finite Automata\": it evolves iterated automata in \
the Mealy, wreath recursion and numeric code presentations, computes the \
level quotients, balls, sections and nucleus of the group they generate, \
searches the group ring for idempotents and zero divisors level by level, and \
draws tree portraits and galleries over automaton and initial-condition space.\
\>", "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->796984843,ExpressionUUID->"360f6590-b427-4416-811c-ef84515b02fd"]
}, Open  ]],

